id     = "osd-bottom-grow"
about  = """A content-sized OSD anchored to the bottom edge grows at scale
1.0 (design.md "Surfaces": an `osd` sized by its content; a content-sized
surface lays out at its new size at once as it grows): a row that springs in
from height 0 above the level label. The
surface grows upward from its anchored bottom edge, so the label at its
bottom never moves on the output, and nothing is drawn past the surface's
edges on any frame (decisions.md eval-rules-3: set E's coverage of
bottom-anchored surfaces resizing). Its shrinking back, and a second growth
over a first, are not here: see decisions.md eval-rules-3 for the open
findings."""
screen = { width = 400, height = 300, scale = 1.0 }

=== shell.strand
state extra = false
osd Level {
  anchor: bottom; margin: 0, 0, 48; open: true
  col { width: 220; pad: 12; gap: 8; radius: 16; bg: #1e1e2ee6
    if extra {
      box { id: more; height: 28; radius: 8; bg: #89b4fa; enter { height: 0; opacity: 0 } }
    }
    row { gap: 8; align: center
      box { id: icon; size: 16; radius: 4; bg: #a6e3a1 }
      text "Volume 40%" { id: head; color: #cdd6f4 }
    }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark grow
set extra true
intend #more enters
rest
expect still #head
expect still #icon
